  "interpretation": {
    "failure_and_retry": "The unchanged state validator rejects Q=0,N>0 with pending=false as failure reason 3 (orphan pair). At gamma=0.5, Q remains positive but below PR85_ICE_NATIVE_INACTIVE_MAX=NEAREST(1.e-14,-1), so the validator skips the ice PSD cone check and accepts positive Q,N. The recorded retry=1 and gamma=0.5 match this source path.",
    "limit": "The run is INCOMPLETE after step 2 and aborts at timestep 3 RK1. Evidence establishes the step-2 cold source sequence and R32 replay for these 13 cells; it is not evidence of full-run completion or global PSD approval.",
    "raw_rate_inference": "The raw Pidep input itself is not in the cold ledger. For the 10 rows where the logged Pidep component matches the full-removal cap times NG alpha, the source equality test would have marked pending if raw Pidep equaled -QI/dt; because no event was recorded, raw Pidep did not equal the cap (and the max-cap implies it was at or below it). The other three rows have a psaci contribution to the aggregate ice-Q removal; their full endpoint is not attributable to Pidep alone. The established cause across all 13 is the total accepted composite endpoint reaching QI=0 with N still positive and the pending flag false.",
    "source_order": "Cold KDM6 sets ice_full_sublimation_pending only when raw pidep is exactly -(qci(2))/dtcld, before max-capping; it then caps with max(pidep,-qci(2)/dtcld). The cold row shows the capped full-removal Pidep, then the near-one NG alpha and outer gamma.",
    "target_rows": "For every target, the exact REAL32 source-order replay of the complete 41-rate vector at gamma=1 produces QI=0 while ice number volume remains positive. The total nongraupel QI request is -QI_before. Ten rows have a Pidep component matching the full-removal cap times NG alpha; three rows also have a positive psaci ice-Q loss contribution, so Pidep alone is below that cap while the aggregate still removes the full ice mass. There is no pending-event row for any target."
  },
